\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Sequence packing and document mask}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{pretraining}

\p{A \newvocab{packed training record} is a tuple
#{\zeta=(x,m,c,M^{\mathrm{doc}})}. It places tokenized segments
#{x^{(1)},\ldots,x^{(r)}} into the length-#{T} token array #{x}, records a
prediction mask #{m}, and records a segment identifier
#{c_t\in\{0,1,\ldots,r\}} at each position. The value #{c_t=0} denotes
padding. Its \newvocab{document mask} is
##{
M^{\mathrm{doc}}_{ts}=
\begin{cases}
0,&c_t=c_s\ne0\text{ and }s\leq t,\\
-\infty,&\text{otherwise}.
\end{cases}
}
Replacing the causal mask in \ref{ftip-000S} by this mask prevents one packed
document from attending to another. We write #{x_t(\zeta)}, #{m_t(\zeta)},
and #{M^{\mathrm{doc}}(\zeta)} for the corresponding fields.}

\p{The prediction mask #{m_t(\zeta)} from \ref{ftip-0015} is one only at
positions whose target token is retained for training. Padding, a segment's
first token when no predecessor is present, and any deliberately excluded
control token receive mask value zero.}
